# No Simulated Functionality

Real interface behaviour is expected: menus open, tabs switch, carousels move, filters filter
the items already on the page, accordions expand, forms validate their own fields.

Anything requiring a backend must not be faked. Never invent balances, order confirmations,
login sessions, activation success messages, live network status, or search results from a
server.

```js
// BAD — pretends the backend did something
button.addEventListener('click', () => {
  showToast('Plan activated successfully!');
});

// GOOD — states the real handoff
<a class="btn" href="https://kabinetim.azercell.com/my/login">Activate in Kabinetim</a>
```

This matches the documented site model: the website is informational and redirect-only. For any
"buy / change / activate" action, show the real handoff — a USSD code, an app deep link, or a
link to the external portal.

Empty and error states may be shown as static examples of that state, clearly labelled, not as
the result of a fake request.
